in those cases you should assume that the returned titles should not be displayed to customers.

args.description:
Cursor for forward pagination. Use the endCursor from pageInfo to fetch the next page.
Each category has its own cursor — when paginating, filter to a single category on the parent field.
Pass the same sort and filter parameters with your cursor to get consistent results.

Example:
    keywordItemCategories(filter: { itemCategories: ["plot-detail"] }, keywordSort: { by: RELEVANCE }) {
      keywords(first: 50, after: "a3cwMDE2Nzcz") {
        pageInfo { endCursor hasNextPage }
        edges { node { text } }
      }
    }

WithNameDataSearchConstraint.description:
The constraints here are combined (AND).

examples:

withNameDataConstraint: {
    allDataAvailable: [TRIVIA],
    noDataAvailable: [TRIVIA]
}
will not match any names.

withNameDataConstraint: {
    allDataAvailable: [TRIVIA, BIRTH_PLACE],
    anyDataAvailable: [BIRTH_DATE, QUOTES]
    noDataAvailable: [DEATH_PLACE]
}
will match names that have (trivia data AND a birth place) AND no death place AND (either a birth date OR quotes).
